0,Trans–New Guinea languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trans–New_Guinea_languages,"Trans–New Guinea is an extensive family of Papuan languages spoken on the island of New Guinea and neighboring islands, a region corresponding to the country Papua New Guinea as well as parts of Indonesia.",Ontenu,Trans-New Guinea
1,Ontenu - ont (Trans-New Guinea) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/ont/,"Ontenu (ont) is part of the Trans-New Guinea family and Trans-New Guinea, Kainantu-Goroka, Kainantu, Gadsup-Auyana-Awa class. Ontenu speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts",Ontenu,Trans-New Guinea
2,Ontenu Language (ONT) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/ont/,Ontenu is an endangered indigenous language of Papua New Guinea. It belongs to the Trans-New Guinea language family. The language is used as a first language by adults only.,Ontenu,Trans-New Guinea
3,An Interview with the Ontenu People of Papua New Guinea - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UmRosEDbq-Y,"Get this update on the Ontenu tribe's challenges to rebuild their village, school and water supply.",Ontenu,Trans-New Guinea
4,Ontenu in Papua New Guinea people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/14203/PP,Constant interaction with other people groups has contributed to a shift towards Tok Pisin. Tok Pisin is one of the national languages of Papua New Guinea. Give thanks to God that their knowledge of Tok Pisin connects the Ontenu people with the rest of the nation and with the scriptures.,Ontenu,Trans-New Guinea
